From: ACK72 <acikom72@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 17:15:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: raise the STA beacon-loss threshold to 20 intervals

The STA beacon monitor reported beacon loss after seven missed beacon
intervals, about 0.77 s with HZ=100. mac80211 then sends two nullfunc
frames back to back and disconnects locally if neither is acknowledged.
An upstream 6 GHz AP was observed skipping beacons and FILS discovery
frames for one to two seconds while it kept serving unicast traffic. A
second client on the same AP lost the same beacons at the same time and
stayed connected, but every gap reaching the monitor cost this station
a reason 4 disconnect and a 5-12 s outage.

Wait twenty intervals, about 2.2 s at 100 TU, which is close to the
missed-beacon limit iwlwifi applies before declaring connection loss.
Losing the AP is still detected, about 1.4 s later than before.

diff --git a/package/kernel/mt76/patches/9999-zzzzzzzz-0026-wifi-raise-sta-beacon-loss-threshold.patch b/package/kernel/mt76/patches/9999-zzzzzzzz-0026-wifi-raise-sta-beacon-loss-threshold.patch
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/mt76/patches/9999-zzzzzzzz-0026-wifi-raise-sta-beacon-loss-threshold.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+From: ACK72 <acikom72@gmail.com>
+Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 17:15:00 +0900
+Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: wait 20 intervals before reporting STA beacon loss
+
+The STA beacon monitor reported beacon loss after seven missed beacon
+intervals, about 0.77 s with HZ=100. mac80211 then sends two nullfunc
+frames back to back and disconnects locally if neither is acknowledged.
+An upstream 6 GHz AP was observed skipping beacons and FILS discovery
+frames for one to two seconds while it kept serving unicast traffic. A
+second client on the same AP lost the same beacons at the same time and
+stayed connected, but every gap reaching the monitor cost this station
+a reason 4 disconnect and a 5-12 s outage.
+
+Wait twenty intervals, about 2.2 s at 100 TU, which is close to the
+missed-beacon limit iwlwifi applies before declaring connection loss.
+Losing the AP is still detected, about 1.4 s later than before.
+
+--- a/mt76.h
++++ b/mt76.h
+@@ -379,7 +379,11 @@ enum mt76_wcid_flags {
+ };
+ 
+ #define MT76_N_WCIDS 1088
+-#define MT76_BEACON_MON_MAX_MISS	7
++/* APs can skip beacons for more than a second, e.g. while scanning off
++ * channel, and keep serving the station. Seven intervals turned those gaps
++ * into disconnects; twenty is close to the limit other clients use.
++ */
++#define MT76_BEACON_MON_MAX_MISS	20
+ 
+ /* stored in ieee80211_tx_info::hw_queue */
+ #define MT_TX_HW_QUEUE_PHY		GENMASK(3, 2)
